<p>British Prime Minister Keir Starmer faced a threatened Labour leadership challenge after former minister Catherine West said she would try to trigger a contest on Monday, May 11, if cabinet ministers did not act against him first. West said she would seek the required Labour MP nominations and take the matter to the Labour Party chair, and the Financial Times reported that she said she had 10 backers. The pressure followed local and regional elections held on Thursday, May 7, in which Labour suffered heavy losses across Britain. Labour lost more than 1,400 council seats in England, reports said; Dawn reported that Nigel Farage&#x27;s Reform UK gained more than 700 council seats in England; and Politico said Labour failed to dislodge the Scottish National Party in Scotland and lost Wales to Plaid Cymru for the first time in more than a century. Starmer rejected calls to resign, wrote in The Guardian that listening to voters did not mean &quot;tacking right or left,&quot; and said he would not &quot;walk away&quot; or &quot;plunge the country into chaos&quot;. He appointed former Prime Minister Gordon Brown as a special envoy on global finance, and reports said Starmer planned a major speech on Monday before the King&#x27;s Speech on Wednesday, May 13.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JtYRv7uTrvhUKxy2L1b-M9t6XmY2mcvcJdSaxrq-asX5AYvX_v3BLKB1Xe5dCXQpXCTJstqDZLfBDMYnCI8xspn4lrbvxdjkv6xwSfW-4v1w' alt='Britain&#x27;s Prime Minister Keir Starmer arrives for a press conference at Downing Street in London, Britain, April 1, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Contest mechanics: A challenger to a sitting Labour leader needs nominations from 20% of Labour MPs, a threshold reported as 81 MPs in the current parliamentary party.</li><li>Rival calculations: Politico reported that some Labour figures were watching Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham. His allies expected him to return to Westminster through a by-election triggered by a sympathetic Labour MP&#x27;s resignation.</li><li>Election scale: The National said almost 25,000 candidates were contesting more than 5,000 council seats in England, alongside votes in Scotland and Wales.</li><li>Party warning: Deputy Labour leader Lucy Powell warned challengers not to provoke a leadership contest and said Labour had to win back voters lost to Reform UK and the Greens.</li></ul><blockquote>This afternoon, I would like the cabinet to come around the table and elect a leader amongst themselves. - Catherine West</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Labour figures reacting to West: HuffPost UK quoted one Labour MP saying he was &quot;almost certain&quot; West would get enough support and calling her &quot;a hero.&quot; A cabinet member said she might not get the numbers but that her move &quot;boils the pot.&quot; (<a href='https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/former-minister-calls-on-cabinet-to-oust-keir-starmer-or-she-will-trigger-leadership-election_uk_69ff5f47e4b065a1677e5b15'>HuffPost UK</a>)</li><li>Keir Starmer: Starmer said Labour had not done enough to give people hope for the future and that he intended to set out how the party would rebuild in the coming days. (<a href='https://www.iltempo.it/tv-news/2026/05/09/video/elezioni-gb-starmer-non-intendo-andarmene-e-gettare-paese-nel-caos-47648718/'>Il Tempo</a>)</li><li>Clive Betts: Betts, described as Labour&#x27;s joint longest-serving MP, urged the cabinet to take decisive action on Starmer&#x27;s premiership. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999068/starmer-vows-to-listen-to-voters-after-election-drubbing'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/may/09/may-elections-results-keir-starmer-labour-nigel-farage-reform-uk-politics-latest-news-updates'>Labour MP says she will trigger leadership contest by Monday if cabinet does not launch challenge – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/50dccc39-c004-4687-a90d-297492